ok   GBC multiclass (K=3): estimators_ has K trees per stage and softmax(initial raw) = class priors
ok   GBR squared_error: stage-1 tree fitted to the negative gradient y - init (leaf value = mean residual of the leaf; squared error needs no line search)
ok   GBR predict = init + learning_rate * leaf value
ok   GBR absolute_error: leaf value = argmin_v sum|r_i - v| over the leaf (a median of the leaf residuals; the line search)  (leaf size, value, median interval) [(9, 1.70175, 1.70175, 1.70175), (9, -2.31718, -2.31718, -2.31718), (3, 0.20115, 0.20115, 0.20115)]
ok   GBR quantile(alpha=0.8): leaf value minimises the pinball loss over the leaf residuals (an 0.8-quantile; the line search)
ok   GBR huber(alpha=0.9): leaf value = median(r) + mean(clip(r - median, -delta, delta)) with delta = 0.9-quantile of |y - init| (Friedman 2001; median = lower or linear definition)  [(6, ['lower-median', 'linear-median']), (7, ['lower-median', 'linear-median']), (4, ['lower-median', 'linear-median']), (4, ['lower-median', 'linear-median'])]
ok   GBC log_loss: leaf value = sum(y - p) / sum(p(1-p)) over the leaf (one Newton step, p = prior at stage 1)
ok   GBC log_loss: predict_proba[:,1] = expit(decision_function), decision = init + lr * leaf
ok   GBC exponential: leaf value = sum(y* exp(-y* raw)) / sum(exp(-y* raw)), y* = 2y-1 (Newton step on the exponential loss)
ok   GBC exponential: predict_proba[:,1] = expit(2 * decision_function)
ok   GBC multiclass log_loss: tree k leaf value = (K-1)/K * sum(y_k - p_k) / sum(p_k(1-p_k)) (Friedman's factor kept)
ok   GBC multiclass: predict_proba = softmax(decision_function) and predict = classes_[argmax]
ok   learning_rate: the stage-1 tree is identical for lr=0.1 and lr=0.2 and (predict - init) doubles
ok   GBR staged_predict[i] = init + lr * cumulative sum of the first i+1 trees; last stage = predict
ok   GBR train_score_[i] = mean squared error after stage i on the training data (loss='squared_error', subsample=1)  (train_score_[0] 2.281197)
ok   GBR absolute_error train_score_[i] = mean |y - f_i|
ok   GBR quantile(0.8) train_score_[i] = mean pinball loss
ok   GBR huber train_score_[i] = mean Huber loss (1/2 r^2 if |r|<=delta else delta(|r| - delta/2)) with delta = 0.9-quantile of |y - f_{i-1}| (set before fitting stage i)
ok   GBC binary log_loss train_score_[i] = binomial deviance = 2 * mean log loss  (train_score_[0] 1.047572, logloss 0.523786)
ok   GBC multiclass train_score_[i] = 1 * mean multinomial log loss (NOT the deviance 2*logloss used in the binary case; documented as 'the loss')  (matches factor 1: True, factor 2: False; train_score_[0] 0.875806, logloss 0.875806)
ok   GBC exponential train_score_[i] = mean exp(-(2y-1) * raw_i) (staged_decision_function yields shape (n, 1) as documented)
