---- IsolationForest
ok   IsolationForest max_samples='auto' -> max_samples_ = min(256, n) = 256 for n = 320; = n for n = 100
ok   each isolation tree is built on max_samples_ = 256 rows drawn without replacement (root n_node_samples = 256, bootstrap=False) with max_depth = ceil(log2(256)) = 8
ok   IsolationForest score_samples = -2^(-E[h(x)] / c(256)), h = leaf depth + c(n_leaf) with c(m) = 2(ln(m-1) + euler_gamma) - 2(m-1)/m (c(2)=1, c(1)=0), averaged over the trees  (unsplit leaves with > 2 samples hit: 7870 of 9600 sample-tree pairs)
ok   IsolationForest contamination='auto': offset_ = -0.5 and decision_function = score_samples - offset_
ok   IsolationForest predict = -1 iff decision_function < 0 else +1
ok   IsolationForest contamination=0.1: offset_ = 10th percentile (linear) of the training score_samples; fraction of training outliers ~ 0.1  (offset_ -0.51164, outlier fraction 0.1000)
ok   IsolationForest max_samples=64 (int): trees on 64 rows, normalisation c(64)
ok   IsolationForest random_state: same seed identical scores
---- RandomTreesEmbedding
ok   RandomTreesEmbedding transform: sparse CSR (n, n_estimators * leaves) one-hot of the leaf index per tree (exactly one 1 per tree per row; every leaf has a training sample)  (leaves per tree [7, 8, 8, 7, 8], shape (80, 38))
ok   RandomTreesEmbedding sparse_output=False: dense ndarray equal to the sparse one
ok   RandomTreesEmbedding trees are totally random regression trees on max_depth=3 (each tree <= 8 leaves) fitted without bootstrap (root n_node_samples = n)
---- Forests
ok   RF bootstrap: n draws with replacement per tree, passed as per-row counts (leaf weighted_n_node_samples = multiplicities of the drawn indices; indices from estimators_samples_)  (root n_node_samples 72 = distinct drawn rows)
ok   RF oob_decision_function_ = mean predict_proba over the trees whose bootstrap sample excluded the row; oob_score_ = accuracy of its argmax  (oob_score_ 0.7417)
ok   RF predict = classes_[argmax(mean of the trees' predict_proba)] (soft vote as documented, not the majority vote)  (majority vote disagrees with the mean-probability rule on 5 of 120 samples)
ok   RF feature_importances_ = mean of the trees' normalised impurity importances (each = total weighted Gini decrease per feature / root weight, normalised), sums to 1
ok   RF max_samples=0.3: each tree's bootstrap has [36] rows (root weighted_n_node_samples)  (36.0)
ok   RF max_samples=50: each tree's bootstrap has [50] rows (root weighted_n_node_samples)  (50.0)
   max_samples=0.35 on 105 rows (36.75): root weight 36 (int -> 36, round -> 37; int expected for this version)
ok   RF max_samples float on 105 rows: int(...) from 1.9, round(...) before
ok   RF class_weight='balanced_subsample': per-tree weights n_boot/(K * class counts of the bootstrap sample) (leaf weights = sum of w_c over the drawn rows)
ok   RF class_weight='balanced' (1.9+): realised by drawing the bootstrap with probability proportional to n/(K * class counts of the full y) (RandomState(tree.random_state).choice(n, n, p=w/sum) replicated); the trees then see plain multiplicities  (class-1 fraction in the draws 0.479 vs 0.492 in y)
ok   RF min_impurity_decrease=0.02: every split satisfies N_t/N * (imp - N_tR/N_t imp_R - N_tL/N_t imp_L) >= 0.02 and the trees are smaller  (min decrease 0.0200; nodes 120 vs 416)
ok   RF monotonic_cst=[1,-1,0,0] (1.4+): predictions monotone along the constrained features
ok   RF regressor: predict = mean of the trees; oob_prediction_ = mean OOB prediction; oob_score_ = R^2
ok   RF warm_start: refit with n_estimators 5 -> 8 keeps the first 5 trees unchanged and adds 3
ok   RF random_state: same seed identical, different seed differs
ok   ExtraTrees default bootstrap=False: every tree uses the whole sample (root count n, weight n)
ok   ExtraTrees: each split threshold lies within [min, max] of the feature over the node's samples (random threshold)
ok   ExtraTreesRegressor bootstrap=True, oob_score: oob_prediction_ recomputed from the unsampled rows; oob_score_ = R^2
ok   ExtraTrees feature_importances_ = mean of the trees' importances, sums to 1
ok   ExtraTrees random_state: same seed identical
